  "body": "Found while re-posting the user's `sc_logo.camproj` on main `59e7378b2`, after #2207 (holder beside the shank) and #2212 (#1749, masked 3D Pocket clears open edges) merged.\n\n## What happens\n\nEvery operation was regenerated by name (no cached paths), then verified:\n- 7 of 8 operations verify clean.\n- \"S1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish\" (3D Pocket, re-machining after \"S1 Adaptive rough profile\") generates `ok` in 21 s, but `verify` gives 71 blocking findings, all of one kind:\n\n```\nS1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish: feed moves 3 and 1597 cross in XY at shared depth\nS1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish: feed moves 1598 and 2998 cross in XY at shared depth\nS1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish: feed moves 1598 and 4450 cross in XY at shared depth\nS1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish: feed moves 2999 and 4450 cross in XY at shared depth\nS1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish: feed moves 2999 and 5975 cross in XY at shared depth\n...\n```\n\nThe post is refused. The move numbers repeat in a pattern (about every 1,400-1,500 moves), which suggests one crossing for each level or each pass: for example a link or a first move of a level that crosses the previous level's path at the same Z.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe re-machining pocket posts with no crossing findings, or a real crossing is fixed in the generator. The crossing check must stay active: do not hide the findings.\n\n## To reproduce\n\nThe user's project is on the agent hosts at `~/parts/sc_logo.camproj` (dude) and `~/sc-parts/sc_logo.camproj` (len). Regenerate \"S1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish\" by name (`generate {\"name\": ...}`), then `verify`. Do not use `camcraft-cli process` alone: it reuses cached toolpaths (see #1749).\n\n## Check first\n\n- Whether the crossings come from #2212's mask change (the centres are now a subset of the unmasked centres, so pass rings can split into pieces whose links cross), or were present before and hidden by the earlier refusals (#2199, #1749).\n- Which moves cross: links, entry moves, or cutting passes.\n\nDone means: on this project, the operation verifies with no crossing findings, the post succeeds, and a test pins the cause on a small fixture.\n\nRefs #1749, #2212.\n",
